# Order Management System

## Project Overview
This repo contains a collection of small-scale Python projects developed as part of a university course titled as Software Engineering as part of my B.Ss. in Computer Science.
Each represented project demonstrates core software engineering concepts such as modular design, object-oriented programming, testing practices, and code quality analysis based on different viewpoints.
## Project Overview:
## 1.Order Management System(cs330_04_01.py)

A comprehensive simulation of a retail order management system, applying OOP(Object-Oriented Programming) principles.
Key Features of this project:
    - Product, Cart, Order, and Customer classes with encapsulated logic.
    - Cart and order manipulation with operator overloading and validation.
    - Invoicing and stock tracking implemented as an additional element used in practical cases such as in real life order management tools
    - Unit and acceptance testing under the name of unittest.

## 2.ATM System(cs330_04_2.py)

A refactored ATM simulation using OOP to enhance maintainability and input validation.

Key Features of this project include:
   - PIN authentication and menu-driven interface.
   - Deposit, withdrawal, and account transfer operations.
   - Recursive menu loop with robust errorhandling.
## 3.GitHUb Repo Info Fetcer (cs330_04_03.py)
A CLI-based tool that fetches and displays GitHub repository metadata utilizing the GitHub API( Application Programming Interface) 

Key Features: 
   - REST API integration using the requests library -> simplifies the process of sending HTTP requests, like POST, GET, DELETE, PUT, etc. 
   - Unittesting implemented by the usage of mocks with unittest mocks.
   - Handles invalid input and missing repos gracefully, without complications or (unnecessary higher level of complexity)
   - Demonstrates how to mock external API responses for isolated tests.
## Requirements
- Python 3.9 or later
- Docker (optional, for containerized deployment)

